Huh, maybe we're taking this too far. Consider that {coi} means hello, and
that {coinai} means goodbye, what does {coicu'i} mean?
Also, of course, that attitudinal string doesn't *necessarily* constitute a
greeting or a parting, but in the context of coming across someone on the
street as well as the context of a meeting coming to an end, I think that I
might interpret it that way.

Also, it's so awfully long that no one would ever conceivably use it.

mi'e la tsani mu'o

